    {
      "id": "2d1ui9m",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EMERGENCY PROVISIONS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 352 allows declaration of National Emergency due to war, external aggression, or armed rebellion.",
        "Article 356 provides for President's Rule upon the failure of constitutional machinery in a state.",
        "Article 360 empowers the President to proclaim Financial Emergency if financial stability or credit is threatened.",
        "The 44th Amendment Act introduced strict safeguards to prevent arbitrary emergency declarations.",
        "Emergency provisions temporarily transform India's federal constitutional setup into a unitary one."
      ],
      "id": "7jhafuo"
    },
